0..73 Comment "// Three worlds each draw two fair bits through `std.rand.Eff`, in a body"
74..150 Comment "// that the caller migrates there. The caller elects the world whose draw is"
151..213 Comment "// greatest, or no leader when two draws tie for the greatest."
214..216 Comment "//"
217..294 Comment "// The draws at separate worlds are independent, as separate supports are. So"
295..371 Comment "// the election has the distribution of three independent uniform draws, and"
372..449 Comment "// the exact model gives it exactly. Each world leads with weight `7/32`, and"
450..488 Comment "// no world leads with weight `11/32`."
489..491 Comment "//"
492..569 Comment "// Each `migrate` runs its body at its world, and the host of the run answers"
570..639 Comment "// the body\'s draw. The corpus runs `elected` once for each of the 64"
640..716 Comment "// sequences of answers, and each path weighs `2^-6`. A world leads when its"
717..779 Comment "// draw beats both other draws, which 14 of the 64 paths give."
780..782 Comment "//"
783..859 Comment "// - see: `model/probability/coin-exchange.gandr` — the exact model across"
860..870 Comment "//   tasks"
871..940 Comment "// - see: `model/worlds/twice.gandr` — a migration and its captures"
941..1013 Comment "// - see: `crates/runtime-emitter/src/world.rs` — a body run here, its"
1014..1055 Comment "//   operations offered to the run\'s host"
1057..1093 Comment "// The host interface of randomness."
